.47-.91-.993-1.36-1.565z\" fill=\"currentColor\" /\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e5d:[\"$\",\"$L6d\",null,{\"className\":\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\",\"style\":{\"--shiki-light\":\"#24292e\",\"--shiki-dark\":\"#e1e4e8\",\"--shiki-light-bg\":\"#fff\",\"--shiki-dark-bg\":\"#24292e\"},\"tabIndex\":\"0\",\"icon\":\"$ed\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L6f\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"line\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"style\":{\"--shiki-light\":\"#D73A49\",\"--shiki-dark\":\"#F97583\"},\"children\":\"import\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"style\":{\"--shiki-light\":\"#24292E\",\"--shiki-dark\":\"#E1E4E8\"},\"children\":\" { providers, Contract } \"}],\"$Lee\",\"$Lef\",\"$Lf0\"]}],\"\\n\",\"$Lf1\",\"\\n\",\"$Lf2\",\"\\n\",\"$Lf3\",\"\\n\",\"$Lf4\",\"\\n\",\"$Lf5\",\"\\n\",\"$Lf6\",\"\\n\",\"$Lf7\",\"\\n\",\"$Lf8\",\"\\n\",\"$Lf9\",\"\\n\",\"$Lfa\",\"\\n\",\"$Lfb\",\"\\n\",\"$Lfc\",\"\\n\",\"$Lfd\",\"\\n\",\"$Lfe\",\"\\n\",\"$Lff\",\"\\n\",\"$L100\",\"\\n\",\"$L101\",\"\\n\",\"$L102\",\"\\n\",\"$L103\",\"\\n\",\"$L104\",\"\\n\",\"$L105\",\"\\n\",\"$L106\",\"\\n\",\"$L107\",\"\\n\",\"$L108\",\"\\n\",\"$L109\",\"\\n\",\"$L10a\",\"\\n\",\"$L10b\",\"\\n\",\"$L10c\",\"\\n\",\"$L10d\",\"\\n\",\"$L10e\",\"\\n\",\"$L10f\",\"\\n\",\"$L110\",\"\\n\",\"$L111\",\"\\n\",\"$L112\",\"\\n\",\"$L113\",\"\\n\",\"$L114\",\"\\n\",\"$L115\",\"\\n\",\"$L116\",\"\\n\",\"$L117\",\"\\n\",\"$L118\",\"\\n\",\"$L119\",\"\\n\",\"$L11a\",\"\\n\",\"$L11b\",\"\\n\",\"$L11c\",\"\\n\",\"$L11d\",\"\\n\",\"$L11e\",\"\\n\",\"$L11f\",\"\\n\",\"$L120\",\"\\n\",\"$L121\",\"\\n\",\"$L122\",\"\\n\",\"$L123\",\"\\n\",\"$L124\",\"\\n\",\"$L125\",\"\\n\",\"$L126\",\"\\n\",\"$L127\",\"\\n\",\"$L128\",\"\\n\",\"$L129\"]}]}]}]\n5e:[\"$\",\"$L48\",null,{\"as\":\"h2\",\"id\":\"tracing-withdrawals-from-child-chain-to-parent-chain\",\"children\":\"Tracing withdrawals from child chain to parent chain\"}]\n5f:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"For the protocol-level model behind withdrawals (assertions, outbox, dispute window), see \",\"$L12a\",\". The equivalent \",[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"ERC-20\"}],\" withdrawal flow at the higher level is described in \",\"$L12b\",\".\"]}]\n60:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"To trace a withdrawal, you first need to wrap the transaction receipt in a \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"ChildTransactionReceipt\"}],\" class. You then need to get the emitted log \",\"$L12c\",\" — emitted by the \",\"$L12d\",\" precompile — as it contains the parameter \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"position\"}],\", which is a unique value for each withdrawal and can be used for a search on the parent chain. To do this, you need to parse the log via the \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"arbSysABI\"}],\" to check for the name of the log being \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"L2ToL1Tx\"}],\".\"]}]\n61:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"Then call \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"getChildToParentMessages\"}],\" on the wrapped receipt to check the status of the withdrawal on the parent chain. If the status is not \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"EXECUTED\"}],\", then the withdrawal transaction has not been executed on the parent chain.\"]}]\n62:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"Since this is a withdrawal, the \",[\"$\",\"$L49\",null,{\"title\":\"Assertion\",\"content\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"A bonded claim made by a \",[\"$\",\"$L18\",null,{\"href\":\"/glossary#validator\",\"children\":\"validator\"}],\" about an Arbitrum chain's execution state, posted to the \",[\"$\",\"$L18\",null,{\"href\":\"/glossary#rollup-contract\",\"children\":\"Rollup contract\"}],\". An assertion may propose a new state or may be a step in a \",[\"$\",\"$L18\",null,{\"href\":\"/glossary#challenge\",\"children\":\"challenge\"}],\". Each assertion consumes messages from the \",[\"$\",\"$L18\",null,{\"href\":\"/glossary#sequencer-inbox\",\"children\":\"Sequencer inbox\"}],\". Gaining the right to post assertions requires a large, one-time \",[\"$\",\"$L18\",null,{\"href\":\"/glossary#bonding\",\"children\":\"bond\"}],\", which the poster loses if a competing assertion is confirmed.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"An assertion moves through several states:\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Proposed\"}],\": a validator submits the assertion.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Challenged\"}],\": another validator disputes the assertion, which starts an interactive fraud proof.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Confirmed\"}],\": nobody challenged the assertion within the \",[\"$\",\"$L18\",null,{\"href\":\"/glossary#challenge-period\",\"children\":\"challenge period\"}],\", which is 6.4 days on Arbitrum One. A \",[\"$\",\"$L18\",null,{\"href\":\"/glossary#bold\",\"children\":\"BoLD\"}],\" challenge adds at most one more challenge period.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}]],\"children\":\"assertion\"}],\" containing the withdrawal needs to be confirmed, so there is no point in searching before that assertion has been confirmed. You can estimate this value by parsing the log for \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"ethBlockNum\"}],\" and adding it to the \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"confirmPeriodBlocks\"}],\" which can be retrieved from the parent chain Rollup contract by calling \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"confirmPeriodBlocks\"}],\".\"]}]\n63:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"Then start the search on the parent chain for the transaction that executed the withdrawal. To do so, search the \",[\"$\",\"$L49\",null,{\"title\":\"Outbox\",\"content\":[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"A parent chain contract responsible for tracking \",[\"$\",\"$L18\",null,{\"href\":\"/glossary#l2-to-l1-message\",\"children\":\"child-to-parent chain message\"}],\"s, including withdrawals, which can be executed once they are confirmed. The outbox stores a Merkle root of all outgoing messages.\"]}],\"children\":\"outbox\"}],\" contract using two values from \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"ChildToParentEvent\"}],\" (retrieved by calling \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"getChildToParentEvents\"}],\" on a wrapped receipt) and use its \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"destination\"}],\" and \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"caller\"}],\" values as two search parameters. Then query the contract starting the search at the previous \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"ethBlockNum + confirmPeriodBlocks\"}],\". If the \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"transactionIndex\"}],\" of the emitted log is equal to the position you grabbed before, then this is the transaction that was responsible for executing the withdrawal transaction.\"]}]\n12e:Tb41,\u003csvg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"M14.23 12.004a2.236 2.236 0 0 1-2.235 2.236 2.236 2.236 0 0 1-2.236-2.236 2.236 2.236 0 0 1 2.235-2.236 2.236 2.236 0 0 1 2.236 2.236zm2.648-10.69c-1.346 0-3.107.96-4.888 2.622-1.78-1.653-3.542-2.602-4.887-2.602-.41 0-.783.093-1.106.278-1.375.793-1.683 3.264-.973 6.365C1.98 8.917 0 10.42 0 12.004c0 1.59 1.99 3.097 5.043 4.03-.704 3.113-.39 5.588.988 6.38.32.187.69.275 1.102.275 1.345 0 3.107-.96 4.888-2.624 1.78 1.654 3.542 2.603 4.887 2.603.41 0 .783-.09 1.106-.275 1.374-.792 1.683-3.263.973-6.365C22.02 15.096 24 13.59 24 12.004c0-1.59-1.99-3.097-5.043-4.032.704-3.11.39-5.587-.988-6.38-.318-.184-.688-.277-1.092-.278zm-.005 1.09v.006c.225 0 .406.044.558.127.666.382.955 1.835.73 3.704-.054.46-.142.945-.25 1.44-.96-.236-2.006-.417-3.107-.534-.66-.905-1.345-1.727-2.035-2.447 1.592-1.48 3.087-2.292 4.105-2.295zm-9.77.02c1.012 0 2.514.808 4.11 2.28-.686.72-1.37 1.537-2.02 2.442-1.107.117-2.154.298-3.113.538-.112-.49-.195-.964-.254-1.42-.23-1.868.054-3.32.714-3.707.19-.09.4-.127.563-.132