rison overview\",\"description\":\"Explore the key differences between Arbitrum and Ethereum, including state transition functions, EVM compatibility, gas handling, and block production. Understand what changes when deploying Ethereum dApps to Arbitrum.\",\"icon\":\"$undefined\",\"url\":\"/arbitrum-essentials/arbitrum-vs-ethereum/comparison-overview\",\"$ref\":\"arbitrum-essentials/arbitrum-vs-ethereum/comparison-overview.mdx\"},{\"$id\":\"arbitrum-essentials/arbitrum-vs-ethereum/block-numbers-and-time.mdx\",\"type\":\"page\",\"name\":\"Block gas limit, numbers and time\",\"description\":\"Understand how Arbitrum handles block gas limits, block numbers, and transaction timing differently from Ethereum. Learn about parent chain gas components and block.number behavior on Arbitrum.\",\"icon\":\"$undefined\",\"url\":\"/arbitrum-essentials/arbitrum-vs-ethereum/block-numbers-and-time\",\"$ref\":\"arbitrum-essentials/arbitrum-vs-ethereum/block-numbers-and-time.mdx\"},{\"$id\":\"arbitrum-essentials/arbitrum-vs-ethereum/rpc-methods.mdx\",\"type\":\"page\",\"name\":\"RPC methods\",\"description\":\"Compare Arbitrum and Ethereum RPC method responses, including additional transaction types, fields, and blocks returned by Arbitrum nodes. Covers eth_getTransactionByHash, eth_getBlockByHash, and other JSON-RPC methods.\",\"icon\":\"$undefined\",\"url\":\"/arbitrum-essentials/arbitrum-vs-ethereum/rpc-methods\",\"$ref\":\"arbitrum-essentials/arbitrum-vs-ethereum/rpc-methods.mdx\"},{\"$id\":\"arbitrum-essentials/arbitrum-vs-ethereum/solidity-support.mdx\",\"type\":\"page\",\"name\":\"Solidity support\",\"description\":\"Learn how Solidity behaves differently on Arbitrum compared to Ethereum, including blockhash, block.coinbase, block.number, msg.sender, and other EVM opcode differences for smart contract developers.\",\"icon\":\"$undefined\",\"url\":\"/arbitrum-essentials/arbitrum-vs-ethereum/solidity-support\",\"$ref\":\"arbitrum-essentials/arbitrum-vs-ethereum/solidity-support.mdx